meta {
  name: Daily notification dispatch (internal job)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/internal/khatm/notifications/dispatch
  body: none
  auth: none
}

docs {
  Replaces: the notification-scheduler edge function (daily cron 0 6 * * *
  UTC) + email-notifications edge function. Whether this stays an HTTP
  endpoint or becomes a plain scheduled job inside hikkmah-backend is Zia's
  call — the semantics below are the contract either way.

  Auth: NOT a user endpoint. Internal-only (service token / network policy);
  the current function 401s anything without the service-role key.

  Three scenarios, evaluated daily:
  1. DEADLINE_REMINDER — per active reminder schedule where group end_date ==
     today + days_before; targets JOINED participants with >= 1 incomplete
     assignment.
  2. JUZ_NOT_STARTED — assignments status ASSIGNED, progress 0, assigned > 3
     days ago.
  3. JUZ_STALLED — assignments status IN_PROGRESS, no update > 4 days.

  Channels per recipient: push (Expo Push API today) and email (Resend).
  Email failures must never block push (threat-model US-11 AC-6).

  Dedup (must survive the port exactly):
  - push:  one per (assignment_id, day), recorded as NOTIFICATION_SENT
  - email: one per (participant_id, event_type, day), recorded as EMAIL_SENT
  Both are currently rows in khatm_audit_log; group_id is NOT NULL there.

  Per-recipient email payloads carry that recipient's group name and juz
  number (do not batch across groups with shared fields — that bug produced
  "Time to start Juz undefined" emails and was fixed in commit 4b6cf5e).

  Emails: sender must be a Resend-verified Hikmah address; body deep-link
  scheme must be Hikmah's; each email carries the unsubscribe link (see
  email-unsubscribe.bru). Skip recipients with email_notifications_enabled
  false or no email on file.

  Implementation notes: use src/utils/logger.ts (Pino) — the current
  functions log dispatch failures per recipient without exposing secrets;
  responses must not leak internal error details (audit fix SA-002).
}
